00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:02.389 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  a spirit airlines flight from mccarran  had a stop on its track seconds before  liftoff this happened last night and  passengers were left waiting well into  the early morning hours to get answers  victoria saha joins us from the newsroom  with the ordeal from one passenger  victoria  having something go wrong with your  plane could be the worst nightmare for  many of us when we get on a flight one  passenger on flight 334 on route to  pittsburgh last night says she thought  the plane was already in the air when  she felt it  hit the ground  these are pictures passenger jennifer  allen of las vegas shared with us the  aftermath of her spirit flight slamming  its breaks seconds before takeoff  emergency personnel getting into the  plane to escort passengers out  spear airlines tells us the pilots  decided to not take off due to a  potential maintenance issue the plane  braked safely upon taxing to the gate  the aircraft experienced a flat tire and  that plane was not just taxing i mean we  were  full speed i mean seconds from lifting  off i actually thought we had  even begun to lift off allen says  passengers were left waiting for hours  for a new plane to come but it did not  she rescheduled her flight for later  this evening  the ffaa says the maintenance issue had  to do with the airspeed indicator and  that the pilots thought it would be best  to not fly in that moment the 9 40 p.m  flight from last night took off this  morning close to 10 a.m reporting live  from the newsroom victoria saha 8 news  now

